Chapter: DiskTestRunner
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter StringUtils

 Build.md Phase B, stage 1. The on-disk test runner's DIRECTORY half: mount the
 boot volume, list what is on it, choose ONE entry by name, read the bytes back
 and report. Compiling and running what is chosen is a later stage and is NOT
 here, because the design's own open question, how one program runs another, is
 unanswered: a chapter carrying `opening` can be cited by nothing (CDX3001), so
 this runner cannot pull the compiler in, and no other composition exists yet.

 Every line prints a verdict of its own rather than one summary, because a
 bare-metal boot has no exit code to read: the serial log IS the result, and a
 stage that fails must say which stage.

Section: The Subject

 `SOURCE.SRC` is the name the img plug writes a `-Source` file under, and it is
 the only source name any image carries today. A runner over `codex/test`
 wants a multi-source image, which the img plug cannot yet build.

  runner-subject : Text = "SOURCE.SRC"

Section: Reporting

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

  runner-names : List Text, Integer, Integer -> Text
  runner-names (names) (i) (n) =
   if i >= n then ""
   else (if i == 0 then "" else " ") & list-at names i & runner-names names (i + 1) n

  runner-first-line : Text -> Text
  runner-first-line (t) =
   let nl = text-index-of t "\n"
   in if nl < 0 then t else text-take t nl

Section: Body

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "=== DISK test runner, stage 1 ==="
    vol <- fat16-boot-volume
    print-line-uni ("volume    : bps=" & show (vol.vol-bytes-per-sector) & " ok=" & yn (vol.vol-bytes-per-sector == 512))
    if vol.vol-bytes-per-sector /= 512 then act
      print-line-uni "REFUSED   : no usable FAT16 volume; nothing to list"
      print-line-uni "=== stage 1 done ==="
    end
    else act
    names <- fat16-list-root vol
    print-line-uni ("entries   : " & show (list-length names))
    print-line-uni ("names     : " & runner-names names 0 (list-length names))
    found <- fat16-file-exists vol runner-subject
    print-line-uni ("subject   : " & runner-subject & " present=" & yn found)
    src <- fat16-read-source vol runner-subject
    when src
      is None -> print-line-uni "read      : FAILED"
      is Just (t) -> print-line-uni ("read      : " & show (text-length t) & " chars, first line: " & runner-first-line t)
    print-line-uni "=== stage 1 done ==="
    end
  end

